<bold>Table&#x000a0;8</bold>
</xref>). In particular, FOI was higher in FSHB c.-211G&#x0003e;T T homozygous patients, both in codominant and recessive models (<xref rid="T8" ref-type="table">
<bold>Table&#x000a0;8</bold>
</xref>). Even in this circumstance the rarity of allele T should be taken into account in the interpretation of data.</p><table-wrap position="float" id="T8"><label>Table&#x000a0;8</label><caption><p>Genotypic association tests performed considering each SNP alone for the follicle on oocytes index (FOI).</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model</th><th valign="middle" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Genotype</th><th valign="middle" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">
